## 3. Serverless Cloud & API Infrastructure
The platform is powered by an event-driven serverless cloud architecture natively deployed in AWS Canada Central (ca-central-1):
- Amazon API Gateway HTTP API v2: Entry point routing requests to Node.js 22.x execution environments.
- Amazon DynamoDB: Single-table design with on-demand capacity (PAY_PER_REQUEST), Point-in-Time Recovery (PITR), and AWS KMS AES-256 encryption at rest.
- Amazon Simple Email Service (SES): Verified transactional email infrastructure dispatching dual-route alerts.
- Amazon Bedrock: Dual-lens agentic swarm orchestrating Anthropic Claude 3.5 Sonnet / Haiku and Amazon Nova models with deterministic JSON schema guardrails.
- Google Calendar API: Service account OAuth2 JWT integration querying live freebusy availability and booking consultation sessions.

### Core API Endpoints:
- `POST /api/intake`: Client dossier submission, CRM lead routing, and booking confirmation.
- `POST /api/chat`: LumiBot agentic conversational terminal with autonomous tool execution.
- `GET /api/calendar/availability`: Real-time freebusy availability query for target dates.
- `POST /api/audit`: Real-time SSRF-protected domain audit evaluating AI search discovery.
- `POST /api/voice/concierge`: Inbound sales voice concierge webhook and intake coordination.
- `GET /api/status`: Zero-trust health telemetry probe.

## 4. Security & Compliance Covenants
- Content Security Policy (CSP): Strict meta policy with default-src 'self', object-src 'none', base-uri 'self', and zero unsafe-eval.
- Zero Public Model-Training Guarantee: Client materials, proprietary intake dossiers, and private prompts are strictly excluded from public AI foundation model training datasets.
- Canadian Data Sovereignty: All persistent databases, Lambda execution runtimes, and telephony queues reside in AWS Canada Central (ca-central-1).
